The file patches the real Go source of net/smtp/smtp.go.

1 part of the real file stays outside the subset. StartTLS raises a connection
that already stands to TLS, and it calls tls.Client. The overlay of crypto/tls
holds no such function, because the secure socket of Dart owns the whole
handshake. StartTLS thus reports the cause and sends no command. SendMail
already gives that error to its caller, thus no password reaches a server in
the clear.

